<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s328S">Now <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w2">sutra</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w14">states</span> that there are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w4">three</span> types of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w3">killing</span>: that which <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w7">comes</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s328p6">from</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w5">desiring</span> something, that which <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w10">comes</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s328p9">from</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w8">disliking</span> something, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s328p23">and</span> that which <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w13">comes</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s328p12">from</span> being <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w11">ignorant</span> of things. One may <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s328f21">ask</span> then <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s328f24">whether</span> the various <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w15"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s328m17">paths</span> of <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s328m16">action</span></span> are each <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s328f20">brought to completion</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s328p19">by</span> these three <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s328w18">roots</span> of all non-virtue.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s328p22"><span class="nul">The first dang coordinates the desire item with the next item in this exact three-item list. English expresses this first linkage through its comma after something at96, while the second linkage has and141–144. The null asserts no separate English word for the first conjunction, with its coordination fused into list punctuation; full HGM dang entry8107 expressly includes comma. This is affirmative punctuation recasting, not unresolved occurrence allocation.</span></span></span>
